# AI working state

Globally-useful state only. Detail lives in `state/<track>.md` — see the
index below. Read this file first every session; read a track's state file
only when you are touching that track.

## Latest

**Dependency and toolchain update, 2026-09-02.** Nothing in `require`
moved: hujson and msgpack are current, and coder/websocket upstream is
still v1.8.15, so the `SetWriteDeadline` fork replace in go.mod stays.
The toolchain pin went go1.27.0 -> go1.27.1 — a patch release, and Go's
patch releases are mostly security fixes, which is why `update-deps`
bumps it at all. The `go` directive stays `1.27`: that is the language
version and has no patch to move. `go fix ./...` reported nothing, which
is the expected answer now that 1.27's fix tool *is* the modernizers and
`dcc35d8` already ran them.

**The staticcheck pin came off**, as the comment holding it had said it
would: 2026.2 shipped as v0.8.1, so `@latest` resolves to something that
can read 1.27 export data.

Then **the standalone binary went too, and there is now one linter**.
staticcheck and `unused` run from inside golangci-lint, which
redistributes the same honnef.co/go/tools; running both was two copies of
one analyser. The disagreement that had kept them apart has a cause worth
knowing: `cmd/staticcheck` does not *register* the `quickfix` analysers
without `-debug.run-quickfix-analyzers`, so the QF reports golangci-lint
made are debug output in honnef's own command. `.golangci.yml` sets
`checks: [all, -QF*]`, which is honnef's set in both directions —
golangci-lint's default also drops several `ST` checks this keeps. The
"internal error in importing" grep went with the binary it guarded; that
exit-0 failure was `cmd/staticcheck`'s alone, and golangci-lint reports a
package it cannot type-check as a `typecheck` issue with a non-zero
status.

**`go vet` went the same way**, and `make lint` is now a single command.
golangci-lint's `govet` generates its default analyser set from
`cmd/vet/main.go`, which the diff against `go tool vet help` on 1.27
bears out exactly — plus `inline`, out of `cmd/fix`. Nothing here was
assumed: every claim above was checked against a seeded package before
the step it justified was deleted. Lint, `test-race` and govulncheck
clean. Detail in `state/ci.md`.

